WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.901
Two paths cross in a park. The crossing spot is on both paths. Two lines on a graph meet at a point whose coordinates fit both equations. That point is the intersection.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:28.619
Two unknowns need two equations. Substitution means writing y using x from one equation, and replacing it in the other. That leaves one equation with one unknown.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:38.872
Elimination is the other method. Add or subtract the equations so one letter cancels. Then put the answer back to find the other letter.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:49.238
These questions say the lines meet at a point, find it, or show that it has given coordinates. Sometimes you must find the equations first.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:01:01.380
Step one: write both equations, finding them first if needed. Step two: eliminate one letter, by substitution or by adding and subtracting.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:15.344
Step three: solve for that letter, then substitute back for the other. Step four: check in the second equation, and give a pair. The trap is a slip when multiplying a bracket.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:37.261
January twenty twenty three. A is minus five, three. B is four, nought. C is minus one, five. The line l goes through C, perpendicular to A B, and meets A B at D. Show that D is minus two, two. Three marks.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:49.116
First the line A B. Its gradient is minus three over nine, which is minus one third. Through B, that gives x plus three y minus four equals zero.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:59.906
Next, the line l. It is perpendicular to A B, so its gradient is three. Through C, minus one, five, it is y equals three x plus eight.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:11.571
Step three: substitute y equals three x plus eight into the equation of A B. That gives x plus three, times, three x plus eight, minus four, equals zero.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:21.393
Multiply out: x plus nine x plus twenty four, minus four. That is ten x plus twenty equals zero. So x is minus two.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:38.379
Back in: y is three times minus two, plus eight, which is two. D is minus two, two. Check in A B: minus two, plus six, minus four, is zero. A tempting slip is three times eight written as eight, which gives the wrong x.

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:45.561
So D is minus two, two, as required. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:57.701
A common mistake is stopping at x. A point needs both coordinates. Substitute back to find y, and write the pair.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:22.246
Now you try, from January twenty twenty. A is three, nought. L one is x minus two y plus two equals zero. It meets L two, x minus seven y minus three equals zero, at C. M is the midpoint of A C. Find M. Write your answer, then choose Continue to Answer.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:34.665
Both lines have x with coefficient one, so subtract. L one minus L two gives five y plus five equals zero, so y is minus one.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:46.872
Put y equals minus one into L one: x is minus four. C is minus four, minus one. M is the midpoint of A and C: minus one half, minus one half.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:58.910
The most common wrong answer is a sign slip when subtracting. Minus two y minus minus seven y is written as minus nine y. Watch the double negative.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:06.227
Remember: two equations, eliminate a letter, solve, substitute back, check, and give a pair.
